  "claim": "The novelty and popular song King of the Road was originally recorded by country music artist in November 1964. This country music artist also recorded the song \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\".",
  "evidencia": "Page: Roger Miller. Sentence: Roger Dean Miller, Sr. (January 2, 1936 – October 25, 1992) was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor, best known for his honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs. His most recognized tunes included the chart-topping country and pop hits \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", and \"England Swings\", all from the mid-1960s Nashville sound era.\nPage: King of the Road (song). Sentence: \"King of the Road\" is a song written and originally recorded in November 1964 by country singer Roger Miller.\nPage: Do-Wacka-Do. Sentence: \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" is a song, released in 1965, by American country music artist Roger Miller.",
