        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5def3d62-f223-53a7-b076-29c31e4bc3b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Miller\n- Songs: \"King of the Road\", \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\", \"Dang Me\", \"England Swings\"\n- Topics: Nashville sound, honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Dean Miller, Sr. was born on January 2, 1936, and died on October 25, 1992.\n- Roger Miller was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor best known for honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs.\n- Roger Miller's most recognized songs included the mid-1960s country and pop hits \"King of the Road,\" \"Dang Me,\" and \"England Swings\" from the Nashville sound era.\n- Roger Miller wrote and originally recorded \"King of the Road\" in November 1964.\n- Roger Miller released \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" in 1965.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8597e1ba-22c4-5776-bc84-5218cb2cc777",
        "text": "Page: Roger Miller. Sentence: Roger Dean Miller, Sr. (January 2, 1936 – October 25, 1992) was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor, best known for his honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs. His most recognized tunes included the chart-topping country and pop hits \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", and \"England Swings\", all from the mid-1960s Nashville sound era.\nPage: King of the Road (song). Sentence: \"King of the Road\" is a song written and originally recorded in November 1964 by country singer Roger Miller.\nPage: Do-Wacka-Do. Sentence: \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" is a song, released in 1965, by American country music artist Roger Miller.",
